            <ArticleTitle>Unilateral adrenal hemorrhagic infarction in essential thrombocythemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>461-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1179/2295333715Y.0000000038</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adrenal hemorrhage is a rare disease associated with various conditions. We report a case of a 68-year-old woman with abdominal and back pain. The diagnostic work-up showed a left adrenal gland infarction associated with essential thrombocythemia. Treatment consisted in painkillers and treating the underlying condition in order to prevent further thrombotic events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
